<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hasan Kuchak</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1343">1343</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Little Hasan, Shaikh Hasan-i Kuchak</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hasan Kuchak, 'Little Hasan', was a grandson of the Ilkhanid commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chupan">Chupan</a>. After the death of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> Abu Sa'id in 1335 he seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azerbaijan">Azerbaijan</a> and set up puppet khans such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sati-beg">Sati Beg</a> and Sulayman Khan to legitimise Chupanid rule. He fought the Jalayirid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hasan-buzurg">Hasan Buzurg</a> and was murdered by his wife in 1343.</p></div>
